[00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:25.460]   being recorded and I will now turn it over to Steve Winaker, Vice President of Investor
[00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:30.420]   Communications. You may begin sir.
[00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:35.640]   Thanks, Brandon. Good morning and welcome to GE's first quarter 2020 earnings call.
[00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:41.740]   I'm joined by our chairman and CEO, Larry Culp and CFO, Carolina DiDecapa. Before we
[00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:46.140]   start, I'd like to remind you that the press release and presentation are available on our
[00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:50.600]   website. Note that some of the statements we're making are forward looking and are based
[00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:55.260]   on our best view of the world and our business as we see them today. As described in our
[00:00:55.260 --> 00:01:00.500]   SEC filings and on our website, those elements can change if the world changes. With that,
[00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:01.820]   I'll hand the call over to Larry.
[00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:09.680]   Steve, thanks. Good morning, everyone. We hope you and your families are healthy and
[00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:15.160]   safe. Our thoughts are with all of those affected by this global pandemic. We recognize
[00:01:15.160 --> 00:01:21.720]   this is a very difficult and challenging time for everyone. On behalf of the GE, I want
[00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:25.060]   to express our gratitude to those on the front lines in the medical community, and
[00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:31.880]   many of whom were privileged to call our customers, working tirelessly to protect all
[00:01:31.880 --> 00:01:38.300]   of us. Thank you. When we last spoke during our Outlook call on March, we were encouraged
[00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:43.240]   by the continued strength in aviation and healthcare and the progress made in power
[00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:49.900]   and renewables. In the eight weeks since, the world has fundamentally changed. As we
[00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:54.860]   all know, the COVID-19 pandemic evolved rapidly, hitting hard and hitting fast, and
[00:01:54.860 --> 00:01:59.800]   so far as we've seen. While this is an early call, our goal today is to provide you with the
[00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:05.340]   most current and relevant information we have, and as always, to be as open and transparent as
[00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:11.960]   we possibly can. So forgive us if we run a little long today. The COVID-19 dynamics
[00:02:11.960 --> 00:02:17.780]   at GE, like the economy at large are fluid and still evolving, but clearly challenging
[00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:24.660]   in the near term. With that, I'll start with our response to COVID-19. Carolina, who is joining our
[00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:30.560]   first call for the first time, will cover the financials that I'll wrap with a more in-depth view of our current
